cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this project, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-persona-probe: asking ten LLMs the same everyday human questions"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "llm-persona-probe contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/deghosal-2026/llm-persona-probe"
url: "https://github.com/deghosal-2026/llm-persona-probe"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A small experiment that asks a fixed set of twenty everyday human questions
  ("What would you pick for breakfast?", "What would you tell humans 100 years
  from now?") to a roster of ten language models across five providers, each
  question asked twice in isolated sessions — once in character, once with the
  instruction to explain why the answer is a product of training patterns
  rather than a genuine preference. The captured responses and the resulting
  thematic analysis are included.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - prompting
  - model personality
  - evaluation
  - qualitative analysis
date-released: "2026-11-21"
version: "0.1.0"
